`metrics_memory_budget_pct`` of ``process_memory.memory_admit_base_bytes()`` (cgroup ``memory.max``, else host ``MemTotal``), and ``_MemoryHeadroomGate`` (``metrics_admit_headroom_mib``; ``cgroup_admit_headroom_ok(..., unlimited_uses_host=True)``, host ``MemAvailable`` when the cgroup is unlimited, read at most once a second) must pass. Nothing in flight always admits one ref (a job larger than the budget runs alone). ``pop_fresh_first`` lets admitted refs skip a refused one until it has waited ``metrics_memory_budget_head_wait_s``; then refs behind it in fresh-first order wait (an aged backfill ref never blocks fresh refs; an aged fresh ref blocks both lanes). The continuous refill runs only once the primary refs are all submitted. Every ref rebuild keeps ``nhosts`` / ``estimated_sample_count`` (``_job_refs_from_jids``, ``_remember_candidate``, deferred refs, strict-ready lookup). Forbidden: count-only admission, or gating on raw ``memory.current`` (page cache). Regression: ``test_primary_fill_respects_memory_budget``, ``test_take_fifo_respects_memory_budget``, ``test_budget_admits_one_when_idle``, ``test_aged_backfill_never_blocks_fresh``, ``test_aged_fresh_blocks_backfill``, ``test_admit_paused_on_headroom``, ``test_artifact_only_counts_full_cost``, ``test_cost_model_learns_denser_jobs_but_never_drops_below_floor``, ``test_measured_frame_size_replaces_the_estimate``, ``test_cost_prices_pivot_grids_linear_in_host_minutes``, ``test_cost_doubling_hosts_at_fixed_per_host_samples_doubles_grid``, ``test_cost_model_learns_denser_grids_but_never_drops_below_floor``, ``test_admission_telemetry_reports_estimated_and_measured`` (``test_metrics_sliding_session.py``); ``test_census_memory_tokens`` (``test_update_metrics.py``, the census ``mem_gib=handoff:,rss:,est:,meas:,budget:`` and ``admit=inflight:,rows_hmin:,grid_b_hmin:`` groups from ``_record_admission_telemetry``); ``test_handoff_size_and_total_bytes_peek_without_taking``, ``test_handoff_size_grid_is_linear_in_hosts_f